{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ad577296-6bdd-46c4-b33f-97c9102d394e","agentId":"ab2005576a43ced02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"The user wants to know two things about Claude Code:\n\n1. Does Claude Code CLI use significantly less memory than the Claude Code Desktop app? (The Desktop app is Electron-based, so presumably heavier. The user wants to free up RAM for a memory-hungry solver process that needs ~40 GiB on a 48 GiB system.)\n\n2. Are conversation histories / sessions shared between Claude Code CLI and Claude Code Desktop? Specifically: if they switch from Desktop to CLI, can they access the same project memories, session transcripts, and continue previous work?\n\nPlease search documentation to give accurate answers. Focus on memory footprint differences and data/history interoperability between the two interfaces."},"uuid":"62db0e30-bbe0-403a-bee6-801bf8d3f2f5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T10:02:05.333Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master"}
